//www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541432/kalen-deboer-says-most-complete-alabama-team","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Can Nebraska's Matt Rhule end his drought against ranked opponents?","description":"Rhule and Nebraska face back-to-back tests against ranked opponents to end the year, marking an opportunity for the Cornhuskers' coach to end a nearly decade-long streak.","published":"2026-11-20T14:02:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534102/nebraska-cornhuskers-matt-rhule-ranked-win-drought","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Florida State going turquoise tops best uniforms of CFB Week 12","description":"The color, which represents harmony, friendship and fellowship throughout Native American communities, pays homage to the school's relationship with the Seminole Tribe.","published":"2026-11-20T14:01:27.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534624/week-12-college-football-uniforms-florida-state","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Connelly on Week 12: Test for Tennessee; Big Ten favorites hit road","description":"Vols, Kiffin meet again and fringe CFP contenders try to stay alive on a sneaky-good Week 12 slate.","published":"2026-11-20T16:00:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532397/connelly-week-12-preview-big-ten-tennessee","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State's club team might be the Buckeyes' most dominant program","description":"One football team in Columbus still has national title hopes. Just not the one with Jeremiah Smith.","published":"2026-11-20T16:21:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522496/ohio-state-club-football","type":"Story","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"'Another universe': How Indiana football changed Bloomington","description":"The basketball haven has become a legend of the fall, where the reigning national champs take center stage.","published":"2026-11-20T16:31:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50533477/bloomington-indiana-football-town","type":"Story","byline":"Chuck Culpepper","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC standardized NIL, revenue sharing contracts 'unfair' for players, agents say","description":"The SEC's new uniform NIL and revenue sharing agreements are causing an uproar among agents concerned that the contracts are loaded with terms that are unfair.","published":"2026-11-20T01:16:03.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535591/sec-standardized-nil-contracts-unfair-players-agents-say","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Waiver approved allowing Army, Navy to play 13th game in 2027","description":"The waiver will allow Army and Navy to play 12 games apiece before the College Football Playoff selections are made and keep their rivalry game.","published":"2026-11-20T14:06:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535192/waiver-approved-army-navy-13th-game-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"James Madison moving to American Conference in 2027","description":"James Madison is leaving the Sun Belt Conference for the American Conference a year earlier than planned, in 2027 rather than 2028.","published":"2026-11-19T21:30:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534149/james-madison-moving-american-conference-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4858848/anto-saka","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anto_Saka"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Anto Saka","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anto_Saka","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:04Z","intro":"Anto Saka (born April 12, 2004) is an American college football defensive end for the Texas A&M Aggies. He previously played for the Northwestern Wildcats.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Saka attended Loyola Blakefield in Towson, Maryland. He was rated as a four star recruit, the fourth overall player in Maryland and the 202nd overall player in the class of 2022. Saka committed to play college football for the Northwestern Wildcats over offers from other schools such as Michigan, Michigan State, Penn State, Tennessee, Toledo, USC, and Wake Forest."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"NORTHWESTERN\nAs a freshman in 2022, Saka was redshirted. In week 2 of the 2023 season, he notched his first career sack in a victory versus UTEP. In week 3 Saka tallied another sack against Duke. He finished the season with 13 tackles, five and a half sacks, and a forced fumble in 11 games played. In 2024, Saka posted 15 tackles with five being for a loss, and three and a half sacks in 11 games.\nOn January 4, 2026, Saka announced that he would enter the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS A&M\nOn January 7, 2026, Saka announced that he would transfer to Texas A&M."}]}}